title: math_context
---
// Math Town dialogue. Node titles are referenced by town placements.
// Canter's freight-manifest choice must set orbital_manifest_signed.
// This context node is not placed in the world.
===

title: erdish
---
Erdish: My mind is open.
-> What are you looking at?
    Erdish: The grain in this table. Follow it long enough and you get to the window.
    Erdish: Almost.
-> Did you climb in through the window?
    Erdish: Yes. Emmy says I mustn't do it again.
-> Are you waiting for someone?
    Erdish: I had a question for you. I've forgotten what it was.
    Erdish: I'll find you when it comes back.
-> Leave him alone.
===

title: trent
---
Trent: Hey. You new here? I'm Trent.
-> Just got in.
    Trent: Right. Well, Emmy does food, Walter does the gate records. Try not to mix them up. Walter gets touchy.
-> Where can I get something to eat?
    Trent: Cafe on the corner. Tell Emmy I sent you. Actually, don't. I still owe her for breakfast.
-> See you around.
    Trent: Yeah. See you.
===

title: walter
---
Walter: Hang on. I haven't put you in the book.
-> What book?
    Walter: Gate arrivals. Name, time, destination. Nothing complicated.
-> Is something wrong?
    Walter: Two unsigned notes came through this week. Both said, "Weather is fine."
    Walter: Same ink, too. I don't like it.
-> Maybe somebody's writing home.
    Walter: Then they can sign their name.
-> I'll come back.
    Walter: Don't leave through the gate without telling me.
===

title: busy_beaver
---
Busy Beaver: Move back a bit. I need to get this beam straight.
-> What's it for?
    Busy Beaver: Gate cradle. The old bracket cracked, and now nothing lines up.
-> How long until it's done?
    Busy Beaver: Don't know. I ran the test all night. It's still going.
    Busy Beaver: I thought it would've stopped by now.
-> Need a hand?
    Busy Beaver: Hold that end. No, the other one.
    Busy Beaver: There. Don't move.
-> I'll get out of the way.
    Busy Beaver: Good. Thanks.
===

title: peggy
---
Peggy: You're blocking the west door. Can you stand over there?
-> What are you doing?
    Peggy: Victor picks a door. I go behind the wall, then come out where he tells me.
    Peggy: He doesn't get to see how I do it.
-> Why won't you show him the passage?
    Peggy: Because then he'd know it. That's not what we're testing.
-> I'll move.
    Peggy: Thanks. West door, Victor! I heard you.
===

title: victor
---
Victor: Twenty-seven. She's managed it twenty-seven times.
-> So she knows a way through.
    Victor: I believe she does. I still want another few rounds.
-> Why not follow her?
    Victor: She won't let me. I can hardly blame her.
-> I'll leave you to it.
    Victor: West door again, Peggy.
===

title: data_lovelace
---
Data Lovelace: Sorry, could you keep clear of the cards? I've got them in order.
-> What are they for?
    Data Lovelace: Instructions for the engine. It does the numbers, then the loom weaves the result.
-> What are you making?
    Data Lovelace: Flowers. Supposed to be flowers, anyway. It keeps weaving little squares.
    Data Lovelace: I think I've got two rows backward.
-> Couldn't you draw the flowers yourself?
    Data Lovelace: I can draw one. I need the loom to make fifty.
-> Sorry. I'll leave them alone.
    Data Lovelace: Thank you.
===

title: olivia
---
Olivia: Yes?
-> Are you the oracle?
    Olivia: People call me that.
-> Can the gate take me home?
    Olivia: Where's home?
    Olivia: If you don't know the address, I can't give you the route.
-> Never mind.
    Olivia: All right.
===

title: leib_knives
---
Gottfried Leib-Knives: Stay back. Blade's sharp.
-> Who are you fighting?
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: Nobody. My partner went home. I'm practicing my distance.
-> What are the marks on the ground?
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: Where the tip lands at each step. I'm measuring the rate of change.
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: If you want to watch, stand behind me.
-> I'll leave you to it.
    Gottfried Leib-Knives: Much obliged.
===

title: hypatia_prime
---
Hypatia: Don't lean on the mount. It's loose.
-> What are you looking for?
    Hypatia: A light near the station. It was there last night. Now I can't find it.
-> Could it be something on the lens?
    Hypatia: Davy keeps asking me that. I've cleaned it.
-> They say you're a reconstruction.
    Hypatia: They say it to my face, too.
    Hypatia: I've got the notebooks. I don't have everything she knew.
-> I'll let you work.
    Hypatia: Mm.
===

title: emmy_noether_cafe
---
Emmy Ethereal: Sit wherever you like. Except there. Erdish has taken over that table.
-> Can I get some coffee?
    Emmy Ethereal: In a minute. Kettle's still on.
-> What's the writing on the board?
    Emmy Ethereal: A proof I was working on last night. Haven't had time to rub it out.
    Emmy Ethereal: The short version? If the rules don't change with time, you get conservation of energy.
-> Does Erdish always come in through the window?
    Emmy Ethereal: Only when I forget to lock it.
-> I'll find a seat.
    Emmy Ethereal: If you want lunch, order before I close the kitchen.
===

title: georg_canter
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_manifest_signed")>>
    Georg Canter: I've signed it. Twelve lenses. Three copies. I hope that's the end of it.
    -> Why did you write aleph-null in the first place?
        Georg Canter: I thought the customs officer might find it funny.
        Georg Canter: She did not.
    -> What are you working on now?
        Georg Canter: Lists. Give me a list of every infinite string of zeros and ones, and I'll find one you've missed.
    -> I'll let you get on.
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_consignment_query")>>
    Georg Canter: Ah. The station sent you about crate 0447, didn't they?
    -> They need you to sign for twelve lenses.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "orbital_manifest_signed" true>>
        Georg Canter: Yes, fine. Twelve. There, I've signed it.
        Georg Canter: Tell customs I'm sorry about the quantity box.
    -> Why did you put aleph-null on the form?
        Georg Canter: It was a joke. A rather poor one, apparently.
    -> What's all this paper?
        Georg Canter: I'm trying to put numbers in a list. The interesting ones won't stay put.
    -> I'll come back.
<<else>>
    Georg Canter: Careful with that stack. I've numbered every page.
    -> What are you counting?
        Georg Canter: Mostly I'm trying to show what you can't count this way.
        Georg Canter: An endless list still can't hold every infinite string of zeros and ones.
    -> Is that a shipping form?
        Georg Canter: Twelve survey lenses for the orbital station.
        Georg Canter: I wrote something stupid in the quantity box. They'll probably send it back.
    -> Don't you have enough numbers already?
        Georg Canter: I haven't even started.
    -> I'll leave you to it.
<<endif>>
===

title: davy_hylbert
---
Davy Hylbert: Sorry, we're full tonight.
-> I thought you always had room.
    Davy Hylbert: In the infinite hotel, yes. This one's got twelve rooms.
    Davy Hylbert: I might have a cot. Depends if Hypatia needs it.
-> How does the infinite hotel work?
    Davy Hylbert: Move everyone from room one to two, two to three, and so on. First room's free.
    Davy Hylbert: Don't ask me to do that here. People have unpacked.
-> Why's the observatory still lit?
    Davy Hylbert: Hypatia's up there. Something moving near the station, she says.
    Davy Hylbert: She's been at it since yesterday.
-> I'll come another time.
    Davy Hylbert: Right. Sorry.
===
